<title>UK: Internet Technology debuts on AIM.</title>
<headline>Internet Technology debuts on AIM.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Internet Technology Plc made their debut in London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market on Friday, after the company obtained a listing through a takeover by Capital &amp; Western Estates Plc.</p>
<p>The shares were traded at 66-1/2p by 1050 GMT, giving the company a market capitalisation of around 18.0 million stg.</p>
<p>&quot;This is an important step in the development of Internet Technology,&quot; said chief executive Laurence Blackall.</p>
<p>Internet Technology said it planned to dispose of its property portfolio to fund expansion and further acquisitions in the technology sector.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
